  "source": "book/assets/c1-make-fact-authoritative.svg",
  "claim": "*One authoritative representation.* BEFORE — copies A, B, C each feed a consumer and can drift apart, so disagreement is possible. AFTER — one authoritative representation, with A, B, C derived or queried from it, so disagreement becomes detectable or impossible.",
  "topology": "Before: three copies of the same fact each feed a separate consumer, and because each copy can\n    change independently, disagreement between them is an ordinary state. After: one authoritative representation\n    carries the fact, and the three consumers derive or query it from that single source, so disagreement becomes\n    detectable or impossible.",
